  "Question": "Machine A produces \\(3/5\\) of all products and has a defect rate of \\(1/10\\); machine B produces \\(2/5\\) and has a defect rate of \\(1/5\\). What is the probability that 1 randomly selected item is defective?",
  "Choices": {},
  "Correct Answer": "7/50",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "Each machine contributes its production share times its defect rate: \\((3/5)(1/10)=3/50\\) from A and \\((2/5)(1/5)=4/50\\) from B. Every defective item comes from exactly one machine, so the required probability is \\(3/50+4/50=7/50\\).",
